# Rclex — Talker / Listener

```elixir
Mix.install(
  [
    {:rclex, github: "FelixPe/rclex"}
  ],
  config: [
    rclex: [
      ros2_message_types: ["std_msgs/msg/String"]
    ]
  ]
)
```

## About

The classic ROS 2 "Hello, world": one node publishes a `std_msgs/msg/String` on
`/chatter`, another subscribes to it.

Reference implementations:

* C++ — [ros2/demos · `demo_nodes_cpp/topics/talker.cpp`](https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/demo_nodes_cpp/src/topics/talker.cpp)
  and [`listener.cpp`](https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/demo_nodes_cpp/src/topics/listener.cpp)
* Python — [ros2/demos · `demo_nodes_py/topics/talker.py`](https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/demo_nodes_py/demo_nodes_py/topics/talker.py)
  and [`listener.py`](https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/demo_nodes_py/demo_nodes_py/topics/listener.py)

You can verify it from another terminal with:

```sh
ros2 topic echo /chatter std_msgs/msg/String
```

## Generate the message types

Run this in a separate cell after `Mix.install/2` has finished.

```elixir
Mix.Task.run("rclex.gen", [])

Application.stop(:rclex)
Application.unload(:rclex)
{:ok, _} = Application.ensure_all_started(:rclex)

alias Rclex.Pkgs.StdMsgs
:ok
```

## Listener

```elixir
Rclex.start_node("livebook_listener")

Rclex.start_subscription(
  fn %StdMsgs.Msg.String{data: data} ->
    IO.puts("[listener] heard: #{data}")
  end,
  StdMsgs.Msg.String,
  "/chatter",
  "livebook_listener"
)
```

## Talker

```elixir
Rclex.start_node("livebook_talker")
Rclex.start_publisher(StdMsgs.Msg.String, "/chatter", "livebook_talker")

# Publish once a second from a Livebook process.
Task.async(fn ->
  for i <- 1..10 do
    msg = struct(StdMsgs.Msg.String, %{data: "Hello world: #{i}"})
    :ok = Rclex.publish(msg, "/chatter", "livebook_talker")
    Process.sleep(1_000)
  end
end)
```

## Cleanup

```elixir
Rclex.stop_subscription(StdMsgs.Msg.String, "/chatter", "livebook_listener")
Rclex.stop_publisher(StdMsgs.Msg.String, "/chatter", "livebook_talker")
Rclex.stop_node("livebook_listener")
Rclex.stop_node("livebook_talker")
```
